From: rtvdb maintainers
Subject: [rtvdb] Drain the Vulkan renderer queue at present

Match the D3D12 renderer's present pacing for the rtvdb Vulkan RT viewer.
After SDL submits the composition command buffer and queues presentation, wait
for that same command buffer's fence before returning to the application.
This keeps the shared graphics queue drained outside the viewer paint callback,
so RT command-slot reuse does not inherit display pacing.

Upstream baseline: SDL release-3.4.10, commit
8e37db5e797b6167f3a00d697d816a684bd259c7. The insertion point is
VULKAN_RenderPresent(), after vkQueuePresentKHR() accepts the current frame
and before currentCommandBufferIndex advances. On an SDL update, retain that
ordering: wait for the fence submitted for the current composition command
buffer, then advance the ring and retain SDL's existing prior-slot reuse wait.
Do not move this wait before vkQueuePresentKHR(), and do not replace it with a
device-wide idle wait; either would change the D3D12-equivalent boundary.

---
 src/render/vulkan/SDL_render_vulkan.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/render/vulkan/SDL_render_vulkan.c b/src/render/vulkan/SDL_render_vulkan.c
--- a/src/render/vulkan/SDL_render_vulkan.c
+++ b/src/render/vulkan/SDL_render_vulkan.c
@@ -4474,6 +4474,31 @@ static bool VULKAN_RenderPresent(SDL_Renderer *renderer)
             SET_ERROR_CODE("vkQueuePresentKHR()", result);
             return false;
         }
 
+        /*
+         * rtvdb uses this renderer with RT commands on the same graphics queue.
+         * Keep the queue-completion wait at present, matching the D3D12 renderer,
+         * rather than deferring display pacing to an application's next command
+         * allocator reuse.
+         */
+        result = vkWaitForFences(
+            rendererData->device,
+            1,
+            &rendererData->fences[rendererData->currentCommandBufferIndex],
+            VK_TRUE,
+            UINT64_MAX);
+        if (result != VK_SUCCESS) {
+            if (result == VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST) {
+                if (VULKAN_HandleDeviceLost(renderer)) {
+                    SDL_SetError("Present failed, device lost");
+                } else {
+                    // Recovering from device lost failed, error is already set
+                }
+            } else {
+                SET_ERROR_CODE("vkWaitForFences()", result);
+            }
+            return false;
+        }
+
         rendererData->currentCommandBufferIndex = ( rendererData->currentCommandBufferIndex + 1 ) % rendererData->swapchainImageCount;
 
         // Wait for previous time this command buffer was submitted, will be N frames ago
